---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why the ABS Dashboard was built, who built it, and how to contribute."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold mb-2">About</h1>
    <p class="text-slate-600 mb-10">Why this exists and how it works.</p>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none space-y-8">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold">The Question</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700 mt-4">
          MLB's 2026 ABS Challenge System gives teams 2 challenges per game to dispute ball-strike
          calls using Hawk-Eye camera data. The obvious question became: do teams that win more
          challenges actually win more games?
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-700 mt-3">
          This dashboard was built to answer that question with real data, not vibes. It tracks
          challenge performance, weights outcomes by game leverage (WPA), and compares challenge
          efficiency to actual win percentage.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold">Why Build This</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700 mt-4">
          Box scores track runs, hits, and errors. No public site was aggregating ABS challenge
          performance in a clean, searchable format and connecting it to standings. This fills that gap.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold">Stack & Open Source</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700 mt-4">
          Built with Astro, Tailwind CSS, Chart.js, and a Python data pipeline powered by
          <code>pybaseball</code>. Data refreshes daily via GitHub Actions and deploys to Cloudflare
          Pages as a fully static site — no servers, no database, no tracking.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-700 mt-3">
          Source code is available on GitHub under the MIT license. Contributions, bug reports,
          and data corrections are welcome.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold">Disclaimer</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700 mt-4 text-sm">
          This site is not affiliated with MLB, any team, or Baseball Savant. All data is sourced
          from publicly available APIs. Metrics are computed independently and may differ from
          official statistics.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
